{"pagination":{"maxPageableSet":"10000","numFound":8,"query":"name=Orwell&limit=10&title=A Collection of Essays","limit":10,"start":0},"items":{"mods":[{"@version":"3.8","titleInfo":[{"nonSort":{"@space":"preserve","#text":"The  "},"title":"collected essays, journalism, and letters of George Orwell"},{"@type":"uniform","@nameTitleGroup":"1","title":"Works. Selections. 1968"}],"name":[{"@nameTitleGroup":"1","@usage":"primary","@type":"personal","namePart":["Orwell, George,",{"@type":"date","#text":"1903-1950"}],"role":{"roleTerm":{"@type":"text","#text":"creator"}}},{"@type":"personal","namePart":"Angus, Ian"},{"@type":"personal","namePart":"Orwell, Sonia"}],"typeOfResource":"text","genre":[{"@authority":"marcgt","#text":"bibliography"},{"@authority":"fast","#text":"Records and correspondence"}],"originInfo":{"place":[{"placeTerm":[{"@type":"code","@authority":"marccountry","#text":"nyu"},{"@type":"text","@authority":"marccountry","#text":"New York (State)"}]},{"placeTerm":{"@type":"text","#text":"New York"}}],"dateIssued":[{"@encoding":"marc","#text":"1968"},[1968]],"issuance":"monographic","agent":{"namePart":"Harcourt, Brace & World"},"edition":["1st ed."]},"language":{"languageTerm":[{"@type":"code","@authority":"iso639-2b","#text":"eng"},{"@type":"text","@authority":"iso639-2b","#text":"English"}]},"physicalDescription":[{"form":{"@authority":"marcform","#text":"print"},"extent":"4 v. facsims., ports. 23 cm."},{"form":{"@type":"Illustrative content","#text":"illustration"}},{"form":{"@type":"Illustrative content","#text":"facsimile"}},{"form":{"@type":"Illustrative content","#text":"portrait"}}],"abstract":{"@type":"Summary","#text":"George Orwell is a major figure in twentieth-century literature. During his lifetime he published ten books and two collections of essays. Orwell seldom \"reported\" and he never took a line other than the one himself felt at the moment of writing. His essays are certainly some of the greatest in that most difficult genre. His widow and her co-editor have collected everything Orwell would have considered an essay, all the journalism that was not purely ephemeral, and those letters which contribute to our understanding of his life and writing. The material is arranged chronologically, and gives a continuous picture of Orwell's life as well as his work. -- From publisher's description."},"tableOfContents":{"@type":"Contents","#text":"v. 1. An age like this, 1920-1940.--v. 2. My country right or left, 1940-1943.--v. 3. As I please, 1943-1945.--v. 4. In front of your nose, 1945-1950."},"note":[{"@type":"statement of responsibility","#text":"Edited by Sonia Orwell and Ian Angus."},{"@type":"bibliography","#text":"Bibliographical footnotes."}],"subject":[{"geographicCode":{"@authority":"marcgac","#text":"e-uk---"}},{"@authority":"lcsh","topic":"Journalists","geographic":"Great Britain","genre":"Correspondence"}],"classification":{"@authority":"lcc","#text":"PR6029.R8 A6 1968"},"relatedItem":[{"@type":"otherFormat","@otherType":"Online version:","@displayLabel":"Online version:","titleInfo":{"title":"Collected essays, journalism, and letters of George Orwell"},"originInfo":{"publisher":"New York : Harcourt, Brace & World, Inc., 1968","edition":"[1st ed.]."},"identifier":{"@type":"local","#text":"(OCoLC)576391017"},"name":{"namePart":"Orwell, George, 1903-1950."}},{"@otherType":"HOLLIS record","location":{"url":"https://id.lib.harvard.edu/alma/990012984430203941/catalog"}}],"identifier":[{"@type":"lccn","#text":"^^^68012591^"},{"@type":"oclc","#text":"366596"}],"location":[{"physicalLocation":{"@displayLabel":"Harvard repository","@type":"repository","@valueURI":"http://id.loc.gov/rwo/agents/no2014094889","#text":"Widener Library, Harvard University"},"shelfLocator":"PR6029.R8 A6 1968"},{"physicalLocation":{"@displayLabel":"Harvard repository","@type":"repository","@valueURI":"http://isni.org/isni/0000000463633307","#text":"Lamont Library, Harvard University"},"shelfLocator":"PR6029.R8 A6 1968"},null,